            <h2>Tips to Save Money on This Route</h2>
            <p>Traveling from Los Angeles to San Diego by train can be budget-friendly with smart planning. Here are some strategies to manage ticket costs without compromising comfort or convenience.</p>
            <h3>Plan for Better Price Options</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Booking tickets early usually secures the lowest fares.</li>
                <li>Prices increase as the travel date approaches.</li>
                <li>Early planning provides more seat options and timing flexibility.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Travel During Off-Peak Hours</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Midday trains are often less crowded and may offer lower fares.</li>
                <li>Avoid peak hours, such as early mornings and late afternoons, to save money.</li>
                <li>Weekdays generally offer more consistent pricing compared to weekends.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Stay Flexible with Your Travel Plans</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Small adjustments to departure times can lead to better ticket prices.</li>
                <li>Considering different train types (express vs local) can open more options.</li>
                <li>Being open to slightly longer travel times can balance cost and convenience.</li>
            </ul>
